From 84bce8e8591776c7c9ad3449d56cbc92a5adbd4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Vogelaar <revogelaar@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:34:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] agent: emit station snapshot topology deltas

OneWifi full associated-client snapshots repeat every current association even
when ownership has not changed. The agent converted every repeated row into a
new sta_list orchestration command and Topology Notification. Each notification
created large controller commands faster than they could be serviced, so the
pending queue retained hundreds of embedded data models and controller RSS grew
without bound.

Reduce full snapshots to association/withdrawal deltas before orchestration.
Refresh unchanged station metrics in the consolidated agent model, remove
unchanged rows from the transient notification model, and drop the command when
no ownership changed. Preserve explicit association plus disassociation rows
for a BSS move.

Add focused tests for repeated identical snapshots and a real BSS move. Also
log pending-queue high-water marks at powers of two so future fan-out is visible
without producing per-command log load.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [RDKB-EM lab validation]
